### activity_list

Read the workspace inbox.

What has happened, newest first.

Filter by namespace to see one kind of thing — tasks, memories, routines — and
by event to see one kind of change. The unread count is always for everything
that matched, not for the page you asked for, so it does not shrink as you page
through.

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "namespace": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Only entries about this kind of thing. Example: \"task\"."
    },
    "event": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Only this event within the namespace. Example: \"status_changed\"."
    },
    "unread": {
      "type": "boolean",
      "description": "Only what you have not read yet."
    },
    "since": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "RFC3339 instant; only entries at or after it."
    },
    "actor": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Whose read state to apply. Defaults to you."
    },
    "limit": {
      "type": "integer",
      "description": "How many to return. Defaults to 50."
    },
    "offset": {
      "type": "integer",
      "description": "How many to skip."
    },
    "_reasoning": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "MANDATORY. NEVER FORGET. Explain why this specific tool is being called now, what outcome you expect, and the immediate next step if that helps clarify the call. Do not leave this empty.",
      "minLength": 1
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "_reasoning"
  ],
  "additionalProperties": false
}
```

### activity_purge

Drop entries past the retention window.

Remove what is older than the retention window, 90 days by default.

Partitions entirely past the window are removed whole. A month only partly
expired is rewritten in place, and the output names which ones — rewriting an
audit log is worth knowing about even when it is correct.

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "olderThanDays": {
      "type": "integer",
      "description": "Override the retention window, in days. Defaults to the configured 90."
    },
    "_reasoning": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "MANDATORY. NEVER FORGET. Explain why this specific tool is being called now, what outcome you expect, and the immediate next step if that helps clarify the call. Do not leave this empty.",
      "minLength": 1
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "_reasoning"
  ],
  "additionalProperties": false
}
```

### activity_read

Mark one entry as read.

Mark one entry read for you.

Read state is per actor and never shared: this changes your inbox and nobody
else's.

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "id": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Identifier of the entry."
    },
    "actor": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Whose read state to change. Defaults to you."
    },
    "_reasoning": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "MANDATORY. NEVER FORGET. Explain why this specific tool is being called now, what outcome you expect, and the immediate next step if that helps clarify the call. Do not leave this empty.",
      "minLength": 1
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "id",
    "_reasoning"
  ],
  "additionalProperties": false
}
```

### activity_read-all

Mark the whole inbox as read.

Move your read watermark to now.

Everything published up to this moment counts as read for you. Anything
published after it does not.

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "actor": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Whose read state to change. Defaults to you."
    },
    "_reasoning": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "MANDATORY. NEVER FORGET. Explain why this specific tool is being called now, what outcome you expect, and the immediate next step if that helps clarify the call. Do not leave this empty.",
      "minLength": 1
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "_reasoning"
  ],
  "additionalProperties": false
}
```

